### **Logical Relationships**

- **G1 -> G2, G3 [AND]**  
  The main goal (delivering resources) requires both **G2 (collection)** and **G3 (delivery)** to be fulfilled sequentially.  
  - **G2 -> AT1, AT2, AT3 [AND]**  
    Collection from a storage involves navigating to the storage location (AT1), requesting resources (AT2), and retrieving them (AT3).  
  - **G3 -> AT4, AT5 [AND]**  
    Delivery to the specified location involves navigating to the delivery zone (AT4) and delivering the resources (AT5).  
  - **AT1 -> AT2, AT3 [AND]**  
    Navigation to the storage location (AT1) must be completed before requesting resources (AT2) and retrieving them (AT3).  
  - **AT5 -> AT6, AT7 [OR]**  
    If the battery is low during delivery (30%), the robot must either return to the checkpoint (AT7) or trigger an alert (AT8).  
  - **AT7 -> AT8 [FALLBACK(AT7, AT8)]**  
    If returning to the checkpoint (AT7) fails, the robot triggers an alert to the sector manager (AT8).  
  - **AT1 -> AT6 [FALLBACK(AT1, AT6)]**  
    If the battery is low during collection (10%), the robot returns to the charging station (AT6) and assigns the task to another robot.  

